//==
// # Model mesh incidence: types (complexity sweep, chunk M2)
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Vertex-to-element incidence

//==
// # Vertex-to-element incidence

// The elements at each vertex of a ModelMesh, in compressed rows: row v is
// Elements[Offsets[v]] up to Elements[Offsets[v + 1]], the elements with a corner at v in
// increasing order, once each; a corner that names no position is in no row. Offsets has one
// entry per vertex plus one, starts at 0 and ends at Elements.Count. The stdlib's
// JaggedArray<ElementIndex> holds the same data, but the C# writer emits no member for a library
// function whose first parameter is an instance of a generic type, so the row accessors need a
// concrete receiver. Removes: the scan of every element per vertex in ComponentsOf and LinkEdges.
type VertexIncidence
    implements IValue
{
    Offsets: Array<Integer>;
    Elements: Array<ElementIndex>;
}
